<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Jan M3 money supply grows 16.89 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Jan M3 money supply grows 16.89 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 16.89 percent in January, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>December M3 growth was revised to 13.62 percent from a preliminary 13.73 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 17.07 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 16.09 percent in December.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economist forecast M3 year-on-year growth of 15.8 percent from 13.7 in December while private credit was seen expanding 15.3 percent against 15.75 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>Jan 1996 preliminary M3 growth -- 16.89 percent</p>
<p>Jan 1996 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 17.07 percent</p>
<p>					   Dec '96	  Nov '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    13.62	    15.18</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  15.76	    18.15</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  30.90	    33.98</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     16.09	    17.13</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand millions)</p>
<p>			    Jan '96(prel) Dec '96 (rev)  Nov '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   319.62	  319.45	   316.12</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    325.94	  317.11	   312.54</p>
<p>Private sector credit 372.95	  367.04	   361.89</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     16.27	   14.74	    14.40</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
